BP 124/76, HR 104 regular, RR 24, SpO₂ 95%, T 36.8. BMI ~29.  
Later (end consult ~11:25): BP 122/78, HR 102, RR 22, SpO₂ 95%.  

Exam (focused):  
Gen: Anxious, talking in full sentences but clearly puffed walking in from waiting room.  
Chest: Mild tachypnoea, chest clear, no wheeze, no focal crackles, good AE, no rub.  
CVS: HS dual, no added sounds, JVP not up, no peripheral oedema, cap refill <2s.  
Calves: L>R mild swelling, non-tender, no erythema/warmth (per previous baseline).  
Abdo: Soft, mild diffuse tenderness only, no peritonism.  

Recent background (from discharge summary 5/52 ago – base hospital):  
- CTPA: segmental PE both lower lobes, mild RV strain  
- Echo: preserved LV, mild RV dilatation  
- Troponin mildly ↑ at that time (demand).  
No new bloods since.  

Impression (messy):  
→ Known PE 6/52 ago, now with ongoing + recently worse exertional dyspnoea, tachypnoea and mild tachycardia. Haemodynamically stable, saturating OK, lungs clear.  
